            <ArticleTitle>Sports injuries in children and adolescents. Questions and controversies.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>727-45</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Certain topics and controversies involving young athletes are addressed, including unclear criteria for volume and intensity of training and acute and overuse injuries of the knee. Osteochondritis dissecans, tibial spine avulsions, peri-pelvic apophyseal avulsions, and back injuries are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
